KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ A under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ M under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ after construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Assertion 1 fails: during A's constructor the call reaches M::id.  Only the
complete object's direct bases with virtual bases get construction vtables
(Itanium C++ ABI 2.6.2); a base-object constructor (M's) leaves the tables
its caller installed instead of installing those of its own bases, for which
the ABI passes a VTT (see cpp_typecheck_constructor.cpp).  With A a direct
base of D, or with V a non-virtual base, the call reaches A::id.
